\hline
\rowcolor{primaryblue!20}
\textbf{Element in} & \textbf{Added} & \textbf{Subtracted} & \textbf{Added back} & \textbf{Net} \\
\hline
Exactly 1 set & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \textcolor{darkgreen}{\checkmark} \\
Exactly 2 sets & 2 & 1 & 0 & 1 \textcolor{darkgreen}{\checkmark} \\
All 3 sets & 3 & 3 & 1 & 1 \textcolor{darkgreen}{\checkmark} \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

\vspace{0.3cm}
\textbf{Memory aid:} Add singles $-$ subtract pairs $+$ add triple.

\vspace{0.3cm}
\textcolor{accentorange}{\textbf{Past Paper:}} 2020 Q1(vi)

\vspace{0.5cm}

Among 200 students: 90 take Discrete Maths (D), 80 take Algorithms (A),
70 take Operating Systems (O). Also: 40 take D and A, 30 take D and O,
20 take A and O, and 10 take all three.

\textbf{(a)} How many take at least one course?

\textbf{(b)} How many take none of the three?

\textbf{(c)} How many take exactly two courses?

\textbf{(d)} How many take exactly one course?

\vspace{0.3cm}
\textcolor{primaryblue}{\textbf{Solution:}}

\vspace{0.2cm}
\textbf{(a)}
\[
    |D\cup A\cup O|
    = 90+80+70-40-30-20+10 = \boxed{160}
\]

\textbf{(b)} $200 - 160 = \boxed{40}$

\textbf{(c)} Exactly two courses (in one pair but not all three):

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{|l|l|}
\hline
\rowcolor{primaryblue!20}
\textbf{Group} & \textbf{Count} \\
\hline
D and A only & $|D\cap A| - |D\cap A\cap O| = 40-10 = 30$ \\
D and O only & $|D\cap O| - |D\cap A\cap O| = 30-10 = 20$ \\
A and O only & $|A\cap O| - |D\cap A\cap O| = 20-10 = 10$ \\
\hline
\textbf{Total exactly two} & $30+20+10 = \boxed{60}$ \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

\textbf{(d)} Exactly one course:

Only D: $90 - 40 - 30 + 10 = 30$

Only A: $80 - 40 - 20 + 10 = 30$

Only O: $70 - 30 - 20 + 10 = 30$

Total exactly one: $30 + 30 + 30 = \boxed{90}$

\textbf{Verify:} $90 + 60 + 10 = 160 = |D\cup A\cup O|$
\textcolor{darkgreen}{\checkmark}

\vspace{0.5cm}

How many integers from 1 to 1000 are divisible by 3, 5, or 7?

\vspace{0.3cm}
\textcolor{primaryblue}{\textbf{Solution:}}

\vspace{0.2cm}
Let $A$ = div by 3, $B$ = div by 5, $C$ = div by 7.

\textbf{Single sets:}
\[
    |A| = \lfloor 1000/3 \rfloor = 333,\quad
    |B| = \lfloor 1000/5 \rfloor = 200,\quad
    |C| = \lfloor 1000/7 \rfloor = 142
\]

\textbf{Pairwise intersections} (use LCM):
\[
    |A\cap B| = \lfloor 1000/15 \rfloor = 66,\quad
    |A\cap C| = \lfloor 1000/21 \rfloor = 47,\quad
    |B\cap C| = \lfloor 1000/35 \rfloor = 28
\]

\textbf{Triple intersection:}
\[
    |A\cap B\cap C| = \lfloor 1000/105 \rfloor = 9
\]

\textbf{By Inclusion-Exclusion:}
\[
    |A\cup B\cup C| = 333+200+142-66-47-28+9 = \boxed{543}
\]

\vspace{0.5cm}

\textcolor{primaryblue}{\textbf{\faLightbulb\ Section 4.4 Summary ---
Inclusion-Exclusion Principle}}

\vspace{0.4cm}
\textcolor{primaryblue}{\textbf{\faCheckCircle\ Core Formulas:}}
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{|l|l|}
\hline
\rowcolor{primaryblue!20}
\textbf{Sets} & \textbf{Formula} \\
\hline
2 sets & $|A\cup B| = |A|+|B|-|A\cap B|$ \\
\hline
3 sets & $|A\cup B\cup C| = |A|+|B|+|C|$ \\
       & $\quad -|A\cap B|-|A\cap C|-|B\cap C|+|A\cap B\cap C|$ \\
\hline
General & Signs alternate: $+$ singles, $-$ pairs, $+$ triples, \ldots \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

\vspace{0.4cm}
\textcolor{primaryblue}{\textbf{\faCheckCircle\ Exact-Count Formulas (3 sets):}}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.5em]
    \item Exactly three: $|A\cap B\cap C|$
    \item Exactly two (e.g.\ A and B only):
          $|A\cap B| - |A\cap B\cap C|$
    \item Exactly one (e.g.\ A only):
          $|A| - |A\cap B| - |A\cap C| + |A\cap B\cap C|$
    \item None: $|U| - |A\cup B\cup C|$
\end{itemize}

